[Music]  i think their passion  you really need it to create something  on a particular level  you need to give everything from  yourself in there  and that's the difference i think  this book means for me that i discuss  really with the client what he wants you  have  ideas here you can see different  materials  different models it's very important to  listen  and nowadays many people don't listen  anymore  the last is really the copy of your foot  on which we create the shoe  but nobody shows you how to make a last  really so you have to  train it by yourself and to get the  feeling by yourself how you should do it  you have certain measurements from the  foot but the feeling of the client  is always different  i love using the leather because you you  get this  particular different touches  what i appreciate so much from this  tannery is they use a swiss cart  maybe it's because it's cold and these  animals live  on a very high level in the mountains  it's always a cow but  cows are also different i think it's  something which you can wear  for a long time and the leather the more  you wear it  it really gets more life i think  i will draw the model from the client  and  this drawing i will translate then on a  flat  paper model which i put on the leather  and we sew it together and from there we  start creating really  the shoe  i think the hand craft and this  concentration of different  craftsmanships in florence is really  um coming up from the medici family  if it's a jeweler or if it's a painter  or  a sculpture maker they always try to  to get the best artisans in town  the upper will be nailed and pulled over  the last  i will start sewing with linen thread  which is  made kind of waterproof with wax when  you stitch  you have two threads which go into the  same hole  and as you pull the wax goes hot it will  seal together  so the water cannot go through and this  is a very particular and very old  process  it's very rare to be a woman in this  shoemaking world  when i started everybody looked at me  and said this lady is going to close  down in a year  a woman in a man's job it's not going to  work and  now they're all proud in the in this  area that i'm still here  we fill in the wooden shank and the back  support because that is the part  under the curve of your foot which will  not be bent  so it has to be supportive and stiff  the front part we will fill with cork  this is to give you a bit of cushion  effect as you bend it the whole time  it's important to have it soft  we apply the sole we will glue it on  and afterwards make a channel we will  stitch  the weld and the leather sole together  through the channel  so it gets more shape of the shoe and  you see it more as a finished product  when we work normally in the workshop  it's a very calm  feeling we are in kind of a meditation  because you are so concentrated on what  you do  you can feel that all of a sudden the  energy comes down  everybody is concentrated on his  particular step  the last big step to put on is the heel  which will be  built out of single layers of leather  we will glue them and nail them on  and then cut them in shape and at the  end we pass some glass  sanding it and then  burn it with hot irons so all the pores  are going to be completely closed up  the last step is to shine the whole shoe  and then we can pull out the last  and then the client can work  [Music]  if you count the hours we would work  around  three weeks on one pair of shoes  when i see a finished shoe and the  client really  tries it on it's always the moment of  reality and relief if it really fits  well  when this person is really happy oh you  can just  see at their eyes without explaining  that that's  the best feeling ever  i think a shoe is more than an object  a shoe really reflects the person who's  wearing it  the leather they choose the color they  choose  and how they wear it because not just  the pear in the beginning it's the pear  over  many many years  you

